{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when you reap.</b> He returned and repeated it, to make them liable on two negative prohibitions. Rabbi Avdimi son of Rabbi Yosef said: What did Scripture see to place it in the middle of the festivals — Pesach and Atzeret on one side, and Rosh HaShanah and Yom HaKippurim and the Festival [of Sukkot] on the other? To teach you that everyone who gives leket, shikhechah, and pe'ah to the poor as fitting — it is accounted to him as though he built the Temple and offered his sacrifices within it (Sifra)." "<b>You shall leave.</b> Leave it before them and they will gather it, and you may not assist any one of them (Pe'ah 5)." "<b>I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> Trustworthy to pay reward."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:59.422172692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}